      or rebranded versions;
   c) compile, build or distribute builds made from this code;
   d) decompile, disassemble, extract resources from, or otherwise reverse
      engineer builds of the Product (including APK and .app), or modify
      and re-sign them;
   e) copy or imitate the Product's visual style — buttons, animations,
      backgrounds, screen layouts, colour themes, logos and names — or
      create visual clones;
   f) use the Product or any part of it for training, sale, rental,
      sublicensing, or as part of other products.

   g) create forks (copies of the repository) in order to use, modify,
      build or distribute them.

   About forks on GitHub. GitHub's Terms of Service let any user press
